Netiquette: Respectful Communication Online
The internet is a social space, and learning to use it well includes understanding netiquette—the informal rules of polite online behavior.
This includes respecting others' opinions, avoiding all-caps messages
(which can read as shouting), thinking before posting, and not sharing others' private information without consent. 
Netiquette also covers the responsible use of emojis, the importance of tone in written communication,
and the value of citing sources when sharing information. Good netiquette fosters healthier online communities and protects users from unnecessary conflict and misunderstanding.
